{"id":"d7584f2b-aaa1-44e0-bf59-e3db9f377867","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"76b6979cf3cbcf27","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/history/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"700afbd8dff54048d3b9626c69edac680c2e65a8","start":4829,"end":5153},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["async","function","textOf","(","path",":","string",")",":","Promise","<","string",">","{","const","open","=","vscode",".","workspace",".","textDocuments",".","find","(","(","document",")","=>","relative","(","document",".","uri",")","===","path",")",";","return","open","?.","getText","(",")","??","Promise",".","resolve","(","vscode",".","workspace",".","fs",".","readFile","(","vscode",".","Uri",".","joinPath","(","root",",","path",")",")",")",".","then","(","(","bytes",")","=>","new","TextDecoder","(",")",".","decode","(","bytes",")",",","(",")","=>","\"","","\"",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"927a1352c91f491d","after":"ab225249fe8e4ea1"}},"payload":{"text":"The text of `path` as it is now: its open document's, or its file's.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:37:02.049Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:37:02.049Z"}
{"id":"eaf24eed-3f8d-4684-9c45-3611209873a7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1e20df20625de121","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/history/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"2d2ffc59457cf2bcfb6cdfe6d4beb55a83fb630e","start":0,"end":63},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","CoverageEvent","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api","\""]},"context":{"after":"f3b75669a67e8f6d"}},"payload":{"text":"History — the program as it stands, read as you edit, and what that changes. When you pause, the program is read by this\nextension's TypeScript server plugin (ts-plugin.js), with the server's own TypeScript, edits not yet saved included.\n\nReplayed against the last reading (util/silo's Replayer), what a pause changed (a feature added, removed, changed, through\nanything it reaches) is told in the History output channel; and what runs say (runs-say.ts), each feature's own code\njoined with the statements this session's runs ran, and a change in that. Its ways in are also what the ledger (ledger.ts)\nis checked against — `silo check`'s drift, in Problems — and what `history.decisions` answers from.\n\nNothing it finds is kept: it's for the session. Once committed, the commit tells what changed (`silo history`).\n\nPublic API only: the plugin through `typescript.tsserverRequest`, and runs through the run contract's `coverage` event. No\nhub, no core capture: the TypeScript server already sees every edit.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:38:14.264Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:38:14.264Z"}
{"id":"ec4495f7-ae03-4c15-acc2-efa110d35b81","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8608fc6b0afbdb40","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/history/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e07184cbc657315f43bb0abd007ed723969977bf","start":14569,"end":14644},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","watcher","=","vscode",".","workspace",".","createFileSystemWatcher","(","\"","**/package.json","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"b1744b3228de4648","after":"ce4c71b104b8f9d3"}},"payload":{"text":"A manifest's ways in change with it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:35:38.014Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:35:38.014Z"}
